  "body": "Follow-up from #3083.\n\n#3083 brings the mill kinds on a mill-turn under the first-traverse laws of a mill. It does not bring the rotary kinds (`Mode::Rotary`, for example `RotaryContour`) under them on a mill-turn.\n\nOn a mill-turn, a rotary kind turns the bar on the spindle C under a radial live tool. The mill premise (an upright tool over an unknown X/Y at the tool-change height) does not apply to that tool. The swept law of #2965 then refuses each such program, for example the shipped C-axis tests (`c_axis_live.rs`, `c_axis_unwind.rs`). So #3083 keeps these kinds out of the law, and decision `docs/decisions/3083-mill-turn-first-traverse.md` records it.\n\nRisk: the first rapid of a radial live-tool rotary operation on a mill-turn can go through the bar, the chuck or the tailstock. No law refuses it. This was also true before #3083.\n\nWork:\n1. Judge the first rapid of a rotary kind on a mill-turn from the turret index position, with the live-tool law of #3077 (`verify::live_first_traverse`), after #3077 merges.\n2. Add pinning tests: one refused case and one clear case.\n\nRelated: #3077, #3083, #2965.\n",
